[node:7e1141c9-91f7-41f7-b82e-53f30246dc1e]
type: concept
tier: mid-term
path: /artifact/the-visual-world-is-the-control-room
created_at: 2026-08-24T10:20:53.210283+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:592add8a-cec4-42ca-bf87-9a8ded2536fc] @ 2026-08-24T10:20:53.210283+00:00

The visual world is “The Control Room”. pmview is the surface a human watches while autonomous agents work. Its job is to let a supervisor scan the whole state of a change-and-memory workflow and act on the one thing that needs them — so the interface stays calm, legible, and out of the way. Hierarchy is carried by weight, tonal panels, and hairline rules rather than color or ornament. The world is light-and-dark twins that share one set of shape, spacing, and motion tokens and swap only their color primitives. Surfaces are flat at rest and depth is a response to intent: cards and list items lift a single pixel with a soft shadow the moment the operator hovers a target.
